WIRE.md §8.1, DECISIONS 229: each copy of an emit json is judged as an out, so an @reload value its first copy writes under another name is E8153, whatever a later copy writes.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A place.
record Place {
  /// Its key.
  id: String
}

/// Every place.
@reload let places: [Place] keyed by id = [{ id: "home" }]

emit json { out: ["@features/a/all.json", "@sovcommon/a/places.json"], values: [places] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8153]  a/a.canon:10:13
  places is emitted in data mode but its file must be places.json

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
